# Staging-only during development

## Local app

- Daily work: `npm run dev` → must use `.env.development` → staging ref `scvojtvgnkmbupvyslmb`.
- Never point `.env.development` or `.env.staging` at production ref `levwrmvqdntngeasrtnb`.
- Run `npm run check:env` before DB-related work.

## Supabase MCP / SQL / migrations

- **Development tasks:** use staging project `scvojtvgnkmbupvyslmb` only.
- **Do not** run `apply_migration`, `execute_sql` DDL, `db push`, or edge function deploy on production unless the user **explicitly** requests a production release.
- Full policy: `.cursor/rules/staging-first-supabase.mdc`.

## Production ref (read-only during dev)

- `levwrmvqdntngeasrtnb` — live Printing Live tracker data (~300 orders). Touch only on explicit user request.
